{"name":"Attic Linen","hex":"#ccbca9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"attic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The space, often unfinished and with sloped walls, directly below the roof in the uppermost part of a house or other building, generally used for storage or habitation.","A storey or a parapet above the cornice of a classical façade, often decorated."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attic"},{"term":"linen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Thread or cloth made from flax fiber.","Domestic textiles, such as tablecloths, bedding, towels, underclothes, etc., that are made of linen or linen-like fabrics of cotton or other fibers; linens."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from linen cloth or thread.","Having the colour linen, light beige."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Attic","blocks":[{"text":"An attic is a space found directly below the pitched roof of a house or other building. It is also known as a sky parlor or a garret. Because they fill the space between the ceiling of a building's top floor and its slanted roof, attics are known for being awkwardly-shaped spaces with difficult-to-reach corners and often exposed rafters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Attic_bedroom.jpg/330px-Attic_bedroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attic","wikidata":"Q244490"},{"title":"Linen","blocks":[{"text":"Linen is a textile made from the bast fibers of the flax plant. Linen cloth has been produced since ancient times primarily for use in clothing and household items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Handkerchief.jpg/330px-Handkerchief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linen","wikidata":"Q1426327"},{"title":"Shades of white","bloc